<article class="env-lemma" id="0H9S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H9S">Lemma <span data-tag="0H9S">12.3.18</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a preadditive category, $x$ and $y$ be objects of $\mathcal{A}$, and $j : y \to x$ and $q : x \to y$ be morphisms satisfying $q \circ j = \text{id} _ y$. If $j \circ q$ has at least one of a kernel or cokernel, then both (co)kernels exist and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \begin{align*}  x &  \simeq \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(j \circ q) \oplus y \\ &  \simeq \mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(j \circ q) \oplus y \end{align*}
</div>
  <p> with the structure of either direct product including $j , q$, and the canonical (co)kernel morphism, and the remaining map uniquely determined. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $f = j \circ q$, compute that $f \circ f = f$, and apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0H9Q" data-tag="0H9Q">12.3.16</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0H9R" data-tag="0H9R">12.3.17</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>